      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research an algorithmic replacement for `bubble_sort`, the current O(cols × rows²) step. Compare suitable general-purpose O(rows log rows) per-column sorts while keeping the column-major layout. Preserve the source’s metric semantics, output format, and numerical behavior; verify median indexing and deterministic mode tie handling. Do not tune to the four observed correctness cases.\",\"B\":\"Research reducing memory traffic in the supplied Problem B implementation. A low-risk candidate is to accumulate each column’s sum and reciprocal sum during input, in the same row order as the current calculation, then share post-sort passes where practical. Initialize all mode-count state; the current `moda_aux` increments malloc’d, uninitialized counters. Preserve the intended mode definition and compare outputs against the reference, including ties and edge cases.\",\"C\":\"Research independent per-column parallelism for the four-core ARM64 target, only if it can use the existing build/runtime setup without changing the compiler or experiment constraints. Measure thread-startup overhead as well as throughput; retain a serial path when parallel overhead outweighs gains. Keep columns independent and output in the original column order, and check numerical and mode behavior against the reference.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidate programs produced by A, B, and C. Run the unchanged correctness and timing evaluation on the fixed ARM64 target, using the same compiler and budget. Measure each candidate and each proposed combination end to end: gains may not be additive, and the supplied baseline is already correct on 4 cases. Keep the fastest fully correct measured integration; reject unmeasured combinations or any that regress correctness or performance.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source is the Problem B descriptive-statistics implementation. Its baseline is valid and correct on 4 observed cases, with mean runtime 0.0093951349457105 seconds (samples 0.0094334921, 0.0094490750, 0.0093028378) on ARM64 with 4 CPU cores. The clearest algorithmic cost is bubble sorting each contiguous column; there are no input dimensions or broader workload measurements to justify assumptions about typical sizes or parallel speedup. Preserve general-input correctness, the reference’s output formatting and metric definitions, and validate all candidate integrations empirically. No commands were run and no files were changed.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"dda33ffc7159e7ae3b6c528a23c32bc7b4ed237e5355662ecbce5106cf7f6536\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research an algorithmic replacement for `bubble_sort`, the current O(cols × rows²) step. Compare suitable general-purpose O(rows log rows) per-column sorts while keeping the column-major layout. Preserve the source’s metric semantics, output format, and numerical behavior; verify median indexing and deterministic mode tie handling. Do not tune to the four observed correctness cases.\",\"B\":\"Research reducing memory traffic in the supplied Problem B implementation. A low-risk candidate is to accumulate each column’s sum and reciprocal sum during input, in the same row order as the current calculation, then share post-sort passes where practical. Initialize all mode-count state; the current `moda_aux` increments malloc’d, uninitialized counters. Preserve the intended mode definition and compare outputs against the reference, including ties and edge cases.\",\"C\":\"Research independent per-column parallelism for the four-core ARM64 target, only if it can use the existing build/runtime setup without changing the compiler or experiment constraints. Measure thread-startup overhead as well as throughput; retain a serial path when parallel overhead outweighs gains. Keep columns independent and output in the original column order, and check numerical and mode behavior against the reference.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidate programs produced by A, B, and C. Run the unchanged correctness and timing evaluation on the fixed ARM64 target, using the same compiler and budget. Measure each candidate and each proposed combination end to end: gains may not be additive, and the supplied baseline is already correct on 4 cases. Keep the fastest fully correct measured integration; reject unmeasured combinations or any that regress correctness or performance.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source is the Problem B descriptive-statistics implementation. Its baseline is valid and correct on 4 observed cases, with mean runtime 0.0093951349457105 seconds (samples 0.0094334921, 0.0094490750, 0.0093028378) on ARM64 with 4 CPU cores. The clearest algorithmic cost is bubble sorting each contiguous column; there are no input dimensions or broader workload measurements to justify assumptions about typical sizes or parallel speedup. Preserve general-input correctness, the reference’s output formatting and metric definitions, and validate all candidate integrations empirically. No commands were run and no files were changed.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"18ddeb645d2a4f99bcfb710c1854674d\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"xhigh\",\"request_sha256\":\"dda33ffc7159e7ae3b6c528a23c32bc7b4ed237e5355662ecbce5106cf7f6536\",\"session_id\":\"fb704484f3a5459ca3a4a358d2208a0b\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"9a6b507c0bb45f30bc7bdf0560eddde4395b25a660e67329e783aed25213f46d\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":12657,\"output_tokens\":4594,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":4117}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"xhigh\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":17251,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
