    {
      "id": 17,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research a faster, correctness-preserving column sort. The source uses bubble sort, which remains quadratic after the measured linear mode scan. Compare a stable O(n log n) sort for columns without NaNs against the existing path, retaining the original comparison and tie behavior; use a safe fallback where needed and keep a small-workload path if measurements justify it. The row-tiled input variant was slower (13.164 ms), so do not assume extra buffering helps.\",\"B\":\"Build on the best measured variant (8.317 ms): retain the sorted-run mode fast path and investigate a subquadratic fallback for columns containing NaNs, where the current implementation retains pairwise comparisons. Preserve equality semantics, earliest-in-order tie selection, float count/mode behavior, and a safe fallback if auxiliary storage fails. Include signed zero and non-finite values in correctness checks; do not keep a faster path that changes printed results.\",\"C\":\"Investigate whether parallel work across independent columns can help on the four-core ARM64 target, with workload-based serial/parallel selection and careful measurement of scheduling overhead. Existing OpenMP sorting (10.768 ms) and fused parallel processing (12.254 ms) were slower than the 9.395 ms baseline; do not reuse their thresholds without evidence or assume fusion and parallelism are additive.\",\"G\":\"Integrate tree outputs incrementally, not by blindly combining edits to the same source file. The best listed result is the mode optimization at 8.317 ms; the measured fused-sum variant is 8.979 ms, while the OpenMP and tiled-input variants were slower. Verify each integrated candidate against the full correctness checks and benchmark the complete program on the target; retain only demonstrated improvements, since combined performance may be worse than either input.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source and statement describe Problem B: seven per-column metrics, sorted columns for median and mode, and one-decimal output. The baseline measured 9.395 ms and was correct on its recorded cases. The strongest measured candidate replaces quadratic pairwise mode work with a sorted-run scan (8.317 ms); accumulating mean and harmonic-mean sums during input also improved time (8.979 ms). Other measured changes regressed, including OpenMP sorting, fused parallel processing, and row-tiled input. Objectives therefore target the remaining sort cost, correctness-sensitive mode edge cases, and cautious parallel evaluation. Every candidate must preserve results for general valid inputs, not just the measured cases.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"9c7f1b2049fa1ad8f5f8d121f8b2926b2d2f9a1a3132f205718304543d711d91\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research a faster, correctness-preserving column sort. The source uses bubble sort, which remains quadratic after the measured linear mode scan. Compare a stable O(n log n) sort for columns without NaNs against the existing path, retaining the original comparison and tie behavior; use a safe fallback where needed and keep a small-workload path if measurements justify it. The row-tiled input variant was slower (13.164 ms), so do not assume extra buffering helps.\",\"B\":\"Build on the best measured variant (8.317 ms): retain the sorted-run mode fast path and investigate a subquadratic fallback for columns containing NaNs, where the current implementation retains pairwise comparisons. Preserve equality semantics, earliest-in-order tie selection, float count/mode behavior, and a safe fallback if auxiliary storage fails. Include signed zero and non-finite values in correctness checks; do not keep a faster path that changes printed results.\",\"C\":\"Investigate whether parallel work across independent columns can help on the four-core ARM64 target, with workload-based serial/parallel selection and careful measurement of scheduling overhead. Existing OpenMP sorting (10.768 ms) and fused parallel processing (12.254 ms) were slower than the 9.395 ms baseline; do not reuse their thresholds without evidence or assume fusion and parallelism are additive.\",\"G\":\"Integrate tree outputs incrementally, not by blindly combining edits to the same source file. The best listed result is the mode optimization at 8.317 ms; the measured fused-sum variant is 8.979 ms, while the OpenMP and tiled-input variants were slower. Verify each integrated candidate against the full correctness checks and benchmark the complete program on the target; retain only demonstrated improvements, since combined performance may be worse than either input.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source and statement describe Problem B: seven per-column metrics, sorted columns for median and mode, and one-decimal output. The baseline measured 9.395 ms and was correct on its recorded cases. The strongest measured candidate replaces quadratic pairwise mode work with a sorted-run scan (8.317 ms); accumulating mean and harmonic-mean sums during input also improved time (8.979 ms). Other measured changes regressed, including OpenMP sorting, fused parallel processing, and row-tiled input. Objectives therefore target the remaining sort cost, correctness-sensitive mode edge cases, and cautious parallel evaluation. Every candidate must preserve results for general valid inputs, not just the measured cases.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"bc2b129be91a43d78cad38607f061287\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"xhigh\",\"request_sha256\":\"9c7f1b2049fa1ad8f5f8d121f8b2926b2d2f9a1a3132f205718304543d711d91\",\"session_id\":\"fb704484f3a5459ca3a4a358d2208a0b\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"2f2f1f39f61922d6056e0d58eedbd6d695a5519198b5663409837fd71608ab01\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":21104,\"output_tokens\":6819,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":6306}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"xhigh\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":27923,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
